 "notes": "Public ResNet-LSTM Foundation_Model (tartan_imu/model/backbones/lstm.py) built with config/resnet_lstm_multihead.yaml (lstm_size=128, lstm_layers=2, lstm_dropout=0.1, drop_ratio=0.3, split_z=True, output_dim=3) and data.imu_freq=200, sample_freq=40, train.seq_len=10. Input is 10 consecutive 1 s windows, each 200 samples @200 Hz decimated by 5 ([::5]) to 40 samples, channels [gyro, acc] in the body frame with gravity (use_local_coord=True). forward(x, predict_cov=False) returns a dict of 4 heads (B,10,3) mean body-frame velocity; predict_cov=True additionally returns log-sigma dict (B,10,3). Parameter shapes do not depend on seq_len, so the IPB wrapper (B,6,T) keeps them unchanged. Registration order: trunk (model.*, including two FcBlocks model.output_block1/2 that the Foundation path never calls), then heads dog, human, car, drone; inside each head nn.Module registers its own Parameter first, so the order is velocity_scale (1,3), output_block1 (2-D xy), output_block2 (3-D log-sigma), output_block1_z (1-D z). param_names are for reference only.",
